From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Yocom <630234+danyocom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 20:15:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] Support the in-game reset in Black Sigil: Blade of the
 Exiled

The game wraps the stock interrupt dispatcher so that interrupts can nest: it
saves SPSR and sets IME on entry, and switches to system mode with irqs enabled
around the handler call. Up to the table lookup it is the stock dispatcher, so
the pattern has to reach past the lookup into the mode switch, which is also
what distinguishes the two.

The jump replaces the two loads before that mode switch rather than the call.
Hooking at the call would run the reset in system mode with interrupts on, where
a handler that interrupts it and waits on the slot 1 lock could deadlock. That
puts the hook ahead of code the game still has to run, so normal dispatch
carries on in the dispatcher itself rather than at the handler, and that code
expects the handler in r0.

Since the reset overwrites r0 while it waits for the lock, the vblank path keeps
the handler in a word of the patch and hands the key check a small stub that
restores it. Nothing can interrupt this code, so a plain word is enough.

Both literal pool offsets are left free in the pattern, and the literal return
address is checked against the location autoload moves the dispatcher to.
